{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/733145-mummy-crossover-question","id":733145,"title":"Mummy crossover question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-27T15:02:05-07:00","id":733145,"title":"Mummy crossover question","content":"In Mummy's Player's Guide there is a top level Effigy ritual that allows you to become a miniture Jesus and be tortured to death to atone for another's sin. This cleans the karmic ledger and even spirits recognize the change as the book specifically mentions how it alleviates spiritual judgements, such as the punishment of heaven lingering over a thief's head or animals forgiving the people who killed them.<br /> <br /> Has anyone considered how this might come into play in a Werewolf game where you are constantly dealing with spirits who have VERY long memories. Perhaps the Mokole and their Innocents, or Bat and his hatred toward the Garou?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T23:25:47-07:00","id":733982,"title":"","content":"I mean, this is kind of off-topic, but that does give some credence to the theory that in cWoD Jesus was Osiris. Huh...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T23:29:29-07:00","id":733984,"title":"","content":"Yes. Also, the Striders kind of liked Jesus and could see he was different. He may have been Osiris after Osiris hit Balance 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T04:38:25-07:00","id":734311,"title":"","content":"... No.<br /> <br /> This is supposed to be a special, unique thing. It requires a special sacrifice and it works on one person, not a whole global culture.<br /> <br /> As for Jesus, he could have been a million different things. Defining it isn't really healthy for the game, though.Actually merging Osiris and all the baggage he carries with all the Judeo - Christian baggage is even worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T16:16:36-07:00","id":736125,"title":"","content":"Nevertheless, if it is used repeatedly, and has enough successes behind it to account for every, or at least MOST of the Innocents, things might get easier for the Mokole. Especially if a Mage gets involved and uses Sorcerer Tikis or some equivalent and special spells before hand to help generate enormous successes. And if this spell were used to for each individual death of the Camazotz... Well this is obviously a long term chronicle idea and is basically just a hypothetical. Still, I think it's interesting to think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T17:17:14-07:00","id":736332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/733145-mummy-crossover-question?p=736125#post736125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nevertheless, if it is used repeatedly, and has enough successes behind it to account for every, or at least MOST of the Innocents, things might get easier for the Mokole. Especially if a Mage gets involved and uses Sorcerer Tikis or some equivalent and special spells before hand to help generate enormous successes. And if this spell were used to for each individual death of the Camazotz... Well this is obviously a long term chronicle idea and is basically just a hypothetical. Still, I think it's interesting to think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing gets better when mages get involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T17:22:04-07:00","id":736344,"title":"","content":"....just because the game allows you to do something &quot;hypothetically&quot; doesn't mean you should do it......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T06:19:08-07:00","id":737881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/733145-mummy-crossover-question?p=736125#post736125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nevertheless, if it is used repeatedly, and has enough successes behind it to account for every, or at least MOST of the Innocents, things might get easier for the Mokole. Especially if a Mage gets involved and uses Sorcerer Tikis or some equivalent and special spells before hand to help generate enormous successes. And if this spell were used to for each individual death of the Camazotz... Well this is obviously a long term chronicle idea and is basically just a hypothetical. Still, I think it's interesting to think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're missing the point. You have people with terrifying secrets and legacies that literally torture them for what their ancestors did. Waving a magical wand to fix things is not the solution. Glorius deeds, grand gestures and sacrifice are how you fix these things.<br /> <br /> Putting in any kind of external solution is cheap and misses the whole point of the narrative element known as &quot;Sins of our Fathers&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T08:52:55-07:00","id":738447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/733145-mummy-crossover-question?p=737881#post737881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're missing the point. You have people with terrifying secrets and legacies that literally torture them for what their ancestors did. Waving a magical wand to fix things is not the solution. Glorius deeds, grand gestures and sacrifice are how you fix these things.<br /> <br /> Putting in any kind of external solution is cheap and misses the whole point of the narrative element known as &amp;quot;Sins of our Fathers&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually thinking of a potential story where a large chunk of the Garou are invited to &quot;sell out&quot; and become meat shields to a bunch of monkey will workers or struggle on and try to find solutions on their own terms. Take the easy way out and become glorified lackies or carry the sins of those who came before you, and maybe hand the will workers their small intestines in a bucket.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T14:07:13-07:00","id":739580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/733145-mummy-crossover-question?p=738447#post738447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was actually thinking of a potential story where a large chunk of the Garou are invited to &amp;quot;sell out&amp;quot; and become meat shields to a bunch of monkey will workers or struggle on and try to find solutions on their own terms. Take the easy way out and become glorified lackies or carry the sins of those who came before you, and maybe hand the will workers their small intestines in a bucket.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just....nope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}